Renew stored offline licenses in the background

`xodus-cli license-refresh --license-cache <dir>` renews every offline
license the signed-in account stored through `run --license-cache`, using
the market each was issued for. An offline lease lasts at most 30 days and
was renewed only by launching that game online, so games played offline for
a while, or not launched at all, lost offline permission even though the
device was online in between. Each renewal follows the launch rules: a new
offline lease replaces the entry, a license without one or a refusal removes
it, and an unreachable Microsoft leaves everything unchanged and ends the
run early. stdout carries one JSON summary line (counts and the earliest new
expiry, no identifiers); the launcher runs it after online game sessions.

